      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, Although the driver still can switch the pin to I2C function with GPIO_ALT_FUNC_1, it will show a warning message if you enable GPIO debug.\nSo please use GPIO_ALT_FUNC_DEFAULT instead.\n\nAlternatively, you can also use the gpio_config_pin() function to switch the pin between GPIO and I2C. With this function, you don\u0027t need to \"hardcode\" the port/pin number here.\nFor example, \n/* Set these two pins to GPIO */\ngpio_config_pin(MODULE_I2C, GPIO_EC_PS2_SCL_TPAD, 0);\ngpio_config_pin(MODULE_I2C, GPIO_EC_PS2_SDA_TPAD, 0);\n/* Restore these two pins to I2C function */\ngpio_config_pin(MODULE_I2C, GPIO_EC_PS2_SCL_TPAD, 1);\ngpio_config_pin(MODULE_I2C, GPIO_EC_PS2_SDA_TPAD, 1);",
